title: Dialogues
---
<<declare $emotion = "neutral">>
===
title: Dialogue_0
color: blue
---
Claire: Finally...
<<wait 0.5>>
Claire: I've been meaning to sit down and knit this scarf for a long time!
<<wait 0.2>>
Claire: A little peace and quiet... 
===
title: Dialogue_1
color: yellow
---
Claire: I think I left the bathroom lights on... 
<<wait 0.3>>
-> Probably not.
	<<set $emotion = "reassurance">>
-> Maybe I should check?
    <<set $emotion = "anxiety">>
===
title: Dialogue_2
color: yellow
---
Claire: Shit, I forgot I had to exercise tonight. It’s been like... two weeks?
<<wait 0.3>>
-> It's fine. I'll do it later...
	<<set $emotion = "reassurance">>
-> Fuck.
    <<set $emotion = "anxiety">>
    Claire: I’m so bad at actually sticking to a schedule. 
    <<wait 0.3>>
    -> Let's pray I actually stick to it this time.
        <<set $emotion = "anxiety">>
    -> Life gets busy sometimes. 
        <<set $emotion = "reassurance">>
===
title: Dialogue_3
color: yellow
---
Claire: Ok, don’t forget the drink at Anne’s tomorrow... might have to bring some wine. Do we have wine?
<<wait 0.3>>
-> Ooh, wine, feelin' like a fancy lady. 
    <<set $emotion = "humor">>
-> Nope, you forgot to buy some again. Damn! 
    <<set $emotion = "anger">>
===
title: Dialogue_4
color: yellow
---
Claire: God, just stop thinking about stuff! How does anyone find knitting relaxing? 
<<wait 0.3>>
-> It's not like I really make anything actually pretty anyway...
    <<set $emotion = "sadness">>
-> They don't. They just pretend so we all feel bad, duh.
    <<set $emotion = "humor">>
===
title: Dialogue_5
color: yellow
---
Claire: For tomorrow’s lunch... I might have some leftovers in the fridge. 
<<wait 0.3>>
-> Are you sure? Maybe you should check?
    <<set $emotion = "anxiety">>
    Claire: I... Ok, I'll check right after.
-> Yeah, you're good.
    <<set $emotion = "reassurance">>
===
title: Dialogue_6
color: yellow
---
Claire: I'll just buy something tomorrow. If I have time.
<<wait 0.3>>
-> Damn, I'll never get a proper break, will I?
    <<set $emotion = "anger">>
    Claire: Ok... One day at a time, Claire.
    <<set $emotion = "reassurance">>
        -> Breathe. 
-> Oh! Maybe we could check out the new Korean restaurant?
    <<set $emotion = "joy">>
===
title: Dialogue_7
color: yellow
---
Claire: Does my eye look weird? It feels weird.
<<wait 0.3>>
-> Girl, you're fine.
    <<set $emotion = "reassurance">>
-> Please, please, please, I can't be sick right now.
    <<set $emotion = "anxiety">>
===
title: Dialogue_8
color: yellow
---
Claire: Maybe Mom was right. If I had worked harder, I probably would have my driver's license by now. 
<<wait 0.3>>
Claire: She never misses a chance to remind me of it. How nice of her. 
<<wait 0.3>>
-> That's actually infuriating.
    <<set $emotion = "anger">>
-> When I do get my license, guess who's not invited in my car?
    <<set $emotion = "humor">>
===
title: Dialogue_9
color: yellow
---
Claire: Fuck, I forgot today was laundry day. 
<<wait 0.3>>
Claire: UGH, I think I don’t have any clean pants for tomorrow. 
<<wait 0.3>>
-> Why am I so bad at remembering things?!
    <<set $emotion = "anger">>
-> It's not the first time I forget this kind of stuff...
    <<set $emotion = "sadness">>
===
title: Dialogue_10
color: yellow
---
Claire: Ok, relax. This is a relaxing time, not an overthinking time. 
<<wait 0.3>>
Claire: Breathe. Why is my chest so tight?
<<wait 0.3>>
-> It's ok, one thing at a time.
    <<set $emotion = "reassurance">>
-> Why do I need a textbook on how to relax?!
    <<set $emotion = "anger">>
===
title: Dialogue_11
color: yellow
---
Claire: Knitting is actually a little harder than I thought.
<<wait 0.3>>
-> Maybe I should just give it up. 
    <<set $emotion = "anxiety">>
    Claire: Like I did with drawing... and pottery...
-> Sweetie, did you really think you could become an expert in 15 minutes?
    <<set $emotion = "humor">>
    Claire: (She giggles).   Yeah, right.
===
title: Dialogue_12
color: yellow
---
Claire: Ok, so laundry... maybe on Wednesday after work? 
<<wait 0.3>>
Claire: No, Wednesday I need to go to the post office, or else they’ll send my package back. 
-> This is so inconvenient. If only I’d done it sooner... 
    <<set $emotion = "anger">>
    Claire: like this afternoon... 
-> Ok, I REALLY need to mark this down. 
    <<set $emotion = "anxiety">>
===
title: Dialogue_13
color: yellow
---
Claire: I had a full afternoon of arts & crafts planned and did nothing but sleep. 
<<wait 0.3>>
Claire: Well done. 
<<wait 0.3>>
-> It's okay. I chose rest today. 
    <<set $emotion = "joy">>
    Claire: Like this afternoon... 
-> I can't help but feel like a failure. 
    <<set $emotion = "sadness">>
===
title: Dialogue_14
color: yellow
---
Claire: GOD, I literally can’t stop thinking. Is it because I haven’t had free time in a long time now? 
<<wait 0.3>>
-> Maybe because my brain isn’t as exhausted from work as it usually is? 
    <<set $emotion = "neutral">>
-> Take it easy. One thought at a time. 
    <<set $emotion = "reassurance">>
===
title: Dialogue_15
color: yellow
---
Claire: I don’t know when I’ll get a free day again... Not in a long time, I think. 
<<wait 0.3>>
-> Should’ve enjoyed it. 
    <<set $emotion = "anxiety">>
-> But in the end... it was a good day, wasn't it? Yes... (she smiles)
    <<set $emotion = "joy">>
===
title: Dialogue_16
color: yellow
---
Claire: With enough practice, I’ll knit a sweater in no time. Or I could make gloves! 
<<wait 0.3>>
-> Cute gloves for the chilly autumn weather... That’s nice. 
    <<set $emotion = "joy">>
-> I could make a scarf for Mom... if she wasn't such a pain to be around. 
    <<set $emotion = "sadness">>
===
title: Dialogue_17
color: yellow
---
Claire: Isn’t rest supposed to feel restful? 
<<wait 0.3>>
Claire: How am I supposed to feel?
<<wait 0.3>>
-> Is it ever possible to stop thinking? 
    <<set $emotion = "neutral">>
    Claire: I think... I hope one day I'll get there.
-> I feel... too much. 
    <<set $emotion = "sadness">>
===
title: Dialogue_18
color: yellow
---
Claire: Note to myself: send a message to Anya; I think she’s been struggling at work recently. 
<<wait 0.3>>
Claire: We should do coffee sometimes. 
<<wait 0.3>>
-> Ok, send it NOW, or else you'll forget.
    <<set $emotion = "anxiety">>
-> It's ok, I'll do it tomorrow. 
    <<set $emotion = "neutral">>
===
title: Dialogue_19
color: yellow
---
Claire: Colette, you're alright dear? (The cat purrs.)
<<wait 0.3>>
-> I wish I could lie in bed all day with you and feel... content. 
    <<set $emotion = "sadness">>
-> You're so CUTE, it's actually unreal. 
    <<set $emotion = "joy">>
===
title: Dialogue_20
color: yellow
---
Claire: (She sighs...)
Claire: I should go to bed now... 
Claire: Ok, tomorrow I’m gonna exercise, do the laundry, call Anya, and contact a driving school.
Claire: All of this preferably before work.
<<wait 0.3>>
-> And after that, maybe I'll take a break. If I have time.  
    <<set $emotion = "anxiety">>
-> Or I could slow down for a bit... sip my tea and let time flow.
    <<set $emotion = "joy">>
    -> Yes, I think I'll like that. 
===